{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable) in a single automaton. The specification automata E1-E4 bind sensor outcomes to safe and efficient actions, enforce recovery after obstacle detection, and prevent repeated identical actions to ensure systematic arena coverage and safety.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception-action logic: plant automaton exposes all sensor and motion events; specifications bind perception outcomes to unique safe actions.",
    "Use helper commit and scan states to ensure one-shot actions and enforce recovery after obstacles, preventing unsafe or oscillatory behaviors."
  ],
